{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you kindle.</b> Why is the section of the Menorah juxtaposed to the section of the princes? Because when Aaron saw the dedication of the princes, his spirit weakened — for he was not with them in the dedication, neither he nor his tribe. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: By your life, yours is greater than theirs, for you kindle and prepare the lamps (see Tanḥuma)." "<b>When you kindle.</b> Because the flame rises, their kindling is written in a term of ascending — that one must kindle until the flame rises on its own (Shabbat 21). And our Sages further expounded from here that there was a step in front of the Menorah, upon which the priest stands and prepares (Sifrei)." "<b>Toward the face of the Menorah.</b> Toward the central lamp, which is not on the branches but on the body of the Menorah (see Menachot 98b)." "<b>Shall the seven lamps cast light.</b> Six that are on the six branches — the three eastern ones face toward the central one, their wicks that are in them — and likewise the three western ones, the heads of the wicks toward the central one. Why? So that one should not say: He needs its light (see Tanḥuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:59.699210816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}